      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### CNN Homemade Model (Spectrograms 2D)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Pc17j3a_B3Cx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "My approach has been to design a simple CNN architecture, one that isn't too large (i.e., doesn't have many parameters) and whose layers aren't too aggressive on the spectrogram. I will test it with raw and pre-processed spectrogram inputs, converting from RGB to GreyScale."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8fuPeUY2EIt0"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "If I add too many layers or make your layers too large, the model will become overly complex and powerful. With a limited dataset like this (len = 1000), this complexity will likely lead to overfitting, resulting in excellent performance on your training set but poor, generalized performance on new data."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gklN0PE-Mbhj"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "I also tried training a TinyVGG architecture from Scratch, but the results were terrible. This model seems to be very aggressive in extracting features, which is not useful with spectrograms."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GQz7hojjFL9x"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "class SpectrogramGenreCNN(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, input_size, num_classes):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Initializes a compact CNN for RGB/Gray spectrograms, designed for efficiency.\n",
        "        :param num_classes: The number of musical genres to classify.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        super(SpectrogramGenreCNN, self).__init__()\n",
        "\n",
        "        # --- Feature Extraction Layers (Convolutional Blocks) ---\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Block 1: Input (1 or 3 channels) to 16 filters\n",
        "        self.conv1 = nn.Conv2d(in_channels=input_size, out_channels=16, kernel_size=3, padding=1)\n",
        "        self.bn1 = nn.BatchNorm2d(16)\n",
        "        self.pool1 = nn.MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Block 2: 16 filters to 32 filters\n",
        "        self.conv2 = nn.Conv2d(in_channels=16, out_channels=32, kernel_size=3, padding=1)\n",
        "        self.bn2 = nn.BatchNorm2d(32)\n",
        "        self.pool2 = nn.MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Block 3: 32 filters to 64 filters\n",
        "        self.conv3 = nn.Conv2d(in_channels=32, out_channels=64, kernel_size=3, padding=1)\n",
        "        self.bn3 = nn.BatchNorm2d(64)\n",
        "        # Note: No final MaxPool here; we use Global Average Pooling later.\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(p=0.4)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # --- Classification Layers (Fully Connected) ---\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Input size is 64 because that is the number of channels (feature maps)\n",
        "        # output by the last convolutional layer (conv3) before GAP.\n",
        "        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(64, 128) # Reduced hidden FC layer\n",
        "        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(128, num_classes) # Final output layer\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Defines the forward pass of the network.\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        # Block 1\n",
        "        x = self.pool1(F.relu(self.bn1(self.conv1(x))))\n",
        "        # Block 2\n",
        "        x = self.pool2(F.relu(self.bn2(self.conv2(x))))\n",
        "        # Block 3\n",
        "        x = F.relu(self.bn3(self.conv3(x)))\n",
        "\n",
        "        # *** Global Average Pooling (GAP) ***\n",
        "        # Reduces the feature maps from (Batch, 64, H, W) to (Batch, 64, 1, 1)\n",
        "        x = F.adaptive_avg_pool2d(x, (1, 1))\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Flatten: x is now (Batch, 64)\n",
        "        x = x.view(x.size(0), -1)\n",
        "\n",
        "        x = self.dropout(x)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # FC Layers\n",
        "        x = F.relu(self.fc1(x))\n",
        "        x = self.fc2(x)\n",
        "\n",
        "        return x"
      ],
